From: pulpoff <pashkovsky@gmail.com>
Subject: Screenshot combo: hide the volume popup instead of destroying it

Destroying the popup's window right after the volume key had brought it up
made phoc drop Phosh's connection ("Error 22 (Invalid argument) dispatching
to Wayland display") and Phosh exited on every power + volume down. The popup
is made fully transparent instead and closes on its own timeout.
---
--- a/src/shell.c	2026-10-10 01:06:18.947294359 +0200
+++ b/src/shell.c	2026-10-10 01:06:18.975098667 +0200
@@ -2825,6 +2825,8 @@
   /* a screenshot is being taken (power + volume down): no volume popup in it */
   if (g_get_monotonic_time () < priv->osd_suppress_until)
     return;
+  if (priv->osd)
+    gtk_widget_set_opacity (GTK_WIDGET (priv->osd), 1.0);
 
   if (priv->osd) {
     priv->osd_continue = TRUE;
@@ -2938,6 +2940,11 @@
   priv = phosh_shell_get_instance_private (self);
 
   priv->osd_suppress_until = g_get_monotonic_time () + msec * G_TIME_SPAN_MILLISECOND;
+  /*
+   * Made invisible, not destroyed: the popup the same key press brought up
+   * may not be configured yet, and destroying its layer surface then made
+   * phoc drop Phosh's connection (EINVAL); its own timeout closes it.
+   */
   if (priv->osd)
-    gtk_widget_destroy (GTK_WIDGET (priv->osd));
+    gtk_widget_set_opacity (GTK_WIDGET (priv->osd), 0.0);
 }
